                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Humorous 2D fighting game where you control ragdoll-like characters, engaging in kung-fu combat using a unique, physics-based control system\n\n✅Ability to design your own characters and add them directly into the game\n✅Rich arsenal of weapons, a slow-motion feature, and the use of magic\n✅Atmospheric soundtrack that complements the dynamic combat\n✅Deep gameplay mechanics that require skill and precision to master\n✅comic-book style graphics\n✅Realistic, fluid ragdoll physics that make encounters dynamic\n✅Good price point\n\n❌ Includes a multiplayer mode, but there are no players\n\n✅✅✅ Verdict: [strike] Terrible [/strike] , [strike] Bad [/strike] , [strike] Mediocre [/strike] , [strike] Decent [/strike] , [strike] Good [/strike] , [b] Very Good [/b] (Rating scale for short games, retro indie simulators, and similar titles)\n\n[quote]If you'd like to see more of my reviews, you can find them on my\ncurator page:\n[url=https://store.steampowered.com/curator/45994324/admin/reviews_manage/]CuratorKingViking[/url]\nand on my group:\n[url=https://steamcommunity.com/groups/CuratorKingViking]GroupKingViking[/url]\n\nIf you have any questions about my reviews, feel free to ask.\nI'm happy to answer them. All reviews are my own!!\nBest regards, King Viking Bezimienny, Polish Game Reviewer. [/quote]",
